{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he sent the dove.</b> At the end of seven days — for it is written ״וַיָּחֶל עוֹד זְבַעַת יָמִים אֲחֵרִים״, from this you learn that also the first time he waited seven days." "<b>And he sent.</b> This is not a term of dispatching but a term of sending away — he sent her off to go her way, and by this he would see whether the waters had subsided: if she finds rest she will not return to him."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:57.587768834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}